From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mempage4k <mempage4k@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 09:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wgpu-core: one command buffer per pass

Each render or compute pass took two raw command buffers: its own, and
one for the barriers (and discard fixups, query resets) before it,
recorded after the pass and inserted ahead of it. Command buffers cost
on their own on some platforms: on Mali each holds ~0.4 MB of host
memory, allocated and freed as pools are reused (~7 % of a game's CPU
time on a Pixel 8a went to that), and Metal hands each to the kernel and
releases it after completion.

Where the hal encoder can suspend command buffers (wgpu-hal 0005: Metal,
not Vulkan, where passes keep their two command buffers), a
pass's command buffer is suspended at its end, and the barriers before
the next pass go at the end of it: they run in the same order, between
the two passes. Commands recorded between passes resume it too. The last
command buffer is ended when the encoder finishes, and before a deferred
query resolve notes its insertion point (what is recorded later must not
go before the resolve).
---
diff --git a/src/command/compute.rs b/src/command/compute.rs
index 2312e90..b9fb12a 100644
--- a/src/command/compute.rs
+++ b/src/command/compute.rs
@@ -922,14 +922,14 @@ pub(super) fn encode_compute_pass(
     } = state;
 
     // Stop the current command encoder.
-    parent_state.raw_encoder.close().map_pass_err(pass_scope)?;
+    parent_state.raw_encoder.close_pass().map_pass_err(pass_scope)?;
 
     // Create a new command encoder, which we will insert _before_ the body of the compute pass.
     //
     // Use that buffer to insert barriers and clear discarded images.
     let transit = parent_state
         .raw_encoder
-        .open_pass(hal_label(
+        .open_before_pass(hal_label(
             Some("(wgpu internal) Pre Pass"),
             device.instance_flags,
         ))
@@ -951,7 +951,7 @@ pub(super) fn encode_compute_pass(
     // Close the command encoder, and swap it with the previous.
     parent_state
         .raw_encoder
-        .close_and_swap()
+        .close_before_pass()
         .map_pass_err(pass_scope)?;
 
     Ok(())
diff --git a/src/command/mod.rs b/src/command/mod.rs
